  "notes_md": "## Key ideas\n- Gemini 2.0 enables real-time multimodal live streaming and applications.\n- Key features include native audio, image, tool use, spatial and video understanding.\n- The Multimodal Live API allows building apps powered by Gemini 2.0 Flash.\n- Tools like Google Search and code execution can be integrated.\n- Features demonstrated include real-time interruptions and memory summaries.\n\n## Quotes\n- \"The Multimodal Live API lets you build real-time multimodal applications powered by Gemini 2.0 Flash.\" (00:37)\n- \"Multimodal refers to the ability to process and understand different types of data, like text, images, and audio all together.\" (01:00)\n\n## Why it matters for me\nLearning about Gemini 2.0's real-time multimodal live streaming capabilities introduces advanced tool use patterns that could eventually interface with data tools. Exploring these real-time AI agents expands understanding of interactive model deployments.\n\n## Try next\n- Explore the Multimodal Live API in AI Studio to build custom applications.\n- Test real-time interruption and memory features in your own prototypes.",
